<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq"><h3>What if I cannot hang for more than 5 seconds on day one?</h3><p>Start with the regression exercises in the beginner dead hang guide for 1 to 2 weeks before beginning this program. Feet-on-ground and band-assisted hangs are two examples. Assisted hangs take part of your weight. They build the baseline grip strength this 4-week structure assumes.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><h3>Can I do dead hangs every day instead of 3 times per week?</h3><p>A rest day between sessions is the common starting rule. Daily hanging is possible later. This plan uses three sessions a week.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><h3>What should I do if I cannot complete all 3 sets at the target time?</h3><p>Falling 2 to 3 seconds short on the third set is normal and acceptable. Record your actual times and aim for full target times by your next session. Repeat the current week before progressing if you consistently miss by more than 5 seconds.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><h3>What happens after I hit 30 seconds on the 4-week program?</h3><p>The 8-week plan framework suits a comfortable hold of 20 to 30 seconds. If you fell short of 30 seconds, repeat weeks 3 and 4 of the 4-week program until you reach it.</p></div>
